  {
    "title": "A server stops answering",
    "body": "The load balancer calls each server's health check every few seconds. A server that does not answer OK is taken out of rotation. Between the moment a server breaks and the next check, requests sent to it may fail or time out. Some balancers and clients retry them on another server, but only requests that are safe to repeat should be retried. A short check interval finds failures faster but adds checking load; a long one sends more requests to a broken server first.",
